## 🚀 Running the Project

### Option 1 — Google Colab

Open the notebook in Google Colab and run the cells sequentially.

The first dataset-loading execution may download the EMNIST dataset.

### Option 2 — Local Environment

Install the required dependencies:

```bash
pip install tensorflow tensorflow-datasets numpy pillow matplotlib
```

Then open the notebook using Jupyter:

```bash
jupyter notebook
```

and run:

```text
EMNIST_CNN.ipynb
```

---

## 🔍 Checking the Model Summary

After creating the model, run:

```python
model.summary()
```

This displays the individual layers, output shapes, and parameter counts.

You can also retrieve the total number of parameters with:

```python
print(model.count_params())
```

Expected result:

```text
225034
```

